1. WHAT YOU NEED
----------------

Hardware
  - An Amiga with a PiStorm and a Raspberry Pi 4 (or CM4). Tested on an
    A1200 with a Pi 4.
  - The Pi's HDMI output for the picture (the game draws on an RTG screen).

Software
  - Emu68 (tested: 1.1.0-beta.1) with its VideoCore RTG driver.
  - AmigaOS 3.x (tested: 3.2.3) with Picasso96 (or CyberGraphX).
  - A 32-bit RTG screen mode at the size you want to play in. The default
    is 1920x1080: check that Picasso96Mode (Prefs) has a 1920x1080 mode
    with 32-bit depth (16.7 million colours), or play at another size
    (section 4).
  - Plenty of Fast RAM: tested with the 1.8 GB Emu68 gives a Pi 4.
  - About 1.6 GB free on a partition for the game's data, and 30 MB for
    this drawer.
  - ogles2.library 1.3 is included (libs/). If an older ogles2.library is
    installed in LIBS:, the game asks you to update it.

Game data (not included)
  The nine files from the "base" folder of Doom 3 1.3.1:

    File          Bytes         MD5
    pak000.pk4    353,159,257   71b8d37b2444d3d86a36fd61783844fe
    pak001.pk4    229,649,726   4bc4f3ba04ec2b4f4837be40e840a3c1
    pak002.pk4    416,937,674   fa84069e9642ad9aa4b49624150cc345
    pak003.pk4    317,590,154   f22d8464997924e4913e467e7d62d5fe
    pak004.pk4    237,752,384   38561a3c73f93f2e6fd31abf1d4e9102
    pak005.pk4        552,334   2afd4ece27d36393b7538d55a345b90d
    pak006.pk4        218,751   a6e7003fa9dcc75073dc02b56399b370
    pak007.pk4        192,031   6319f086f930ec1618ab09b4c20c268c
    pak008.pk4         12,243   28750b7841de9453eb335bad6841a2a5

  The GOG.com and Steam versions have exactly these files. A boxed copy
  needs the 1.3.1 patch (pak008.pk4 comes from it). "Doom 3: BFG Edition"
  will NOT work: its data is in a different format.

  The free 2004 demo works too: put its demo00.pk4 (483,535,485 bytes,
  MD5 70c2c63ef1190158f1ebd6c255b22d8e) into the demo/ drawer instead.


2. INSTALLING
-------------

  1. Unpack the archive where you want the game, for example to Work:
     (LhA x Doom3-Amiga-@VERSION@.lha Work:). This makes the drawer Doom3.
     It can be anywhere, on any partition.

  2. Copy the nine pak00?.pk4 files into Doom3/base/. On the PC they are
     in the game's installation folder, under "base" (GOG: for example
     C:\GOG Games\Doom 3\base; Steam: ...\steamapps\common\Doom 3\base).
     Copy them over the network, or with a CF or SD card. Only the
     pak*.pk4 files are needed.

  3. If you like, check them on the Amiga: MD5Sum Doom3/base/#?.pk4 and
     compare with the list in section 1. A damaged file makes the game
     stop while loading.

Nothing is copied to your system: ogles2.library and its shader
compiler are taken from Doom3/libs/, the game's compiled shaders from
Doom3/shaders/. Settings and saved games go to Doom3/save/.


3. STARTING THE GAME
--------------------

Double-click the Doom3 icon. The game loads for a while, then its screen
opens with the main menu. Starting a new game loads the first level, which
takes about a minute and a half.

From a Shell:

    Work:Doom3/Doom3
    Work:Doom3/Doom3 QUALITY=medium W=1280 H=720

(the options are in section 4). Doom3 is a small program that runs the
script Doom3.script in its drawer, with the right stack (9 MB) and
settings; it can be started from any directory.

Quit from the game's main menu (Exit), or type "quit" in the console.


4. OPTIONS
----------

Options are given to Doom3 in a Shell (Doom3 KEY=VALUE ...) or as the
icon's Tool Types: select the Doom3 icon, choose Icons > Information,
change a value (e.g. QUALITY=low into QUALITY=medium) and save. The icon
holds the main options at their defaults; the others can be added the
same way. A Tool Type in parentheses, e.g. (QUALITY=high), is ignored.

  W=1920 H=1080     The screen size (a 32-bit RTG mode of that size must
                    exist). Smaller is a little faster.
  QUALITY=low       low, medium or high: the graphics settings (low.cfg,
                    medium.cfg, high.cfg in the drawer). See section 5.
  LIGHTS=12         The most lights drawn in a frame: the nearest and
                    largest ones are kept. Fewer is faster; 0 draws them
                    all (slower, but no lights popping in and out).
  AUDIO=paula       paula (the Amiga's own sound chip, the default) or
                    ahi (through AHI). See section 6.
  SOUND=1           0 turns sound off.
  VOICES=32         The most sounds playing at once.
  RATE=22050        The mixing rate in Hz (Paula plays at most 22050).
  HZ=20             The game's tics a second (20 is smoother here than
                    Doom 3's own 60, which the Amiga cannot keep up with).
  MAP=game/mars_city1
                    Starts straight in a level instead of the main menu.

The game's own menus (Options > System) can change the quality too, but
it takes effect only at the next start, and the QUALITY setting is
applied again at every start: use QUALITY to choose.


5. SPEED AND QUALITY
--------------------

Doom 3 was made for PCs far faster than any Amiga, so expect a playable
but not smooth game. Measured on an A1200 with a Pi 4 (its ARM at
2.2 GHz):

  Doom 3's own benchmark (timedemo demo1, a busy scene):
    1920x1080, QUALITY=low, LIGHTS=12      16.9 frames a second
  The port's own benchmark (a quieter scene):
    1920x1080, QUALITY=low, LIGHTS=12      21 frames a second
    640x480,   QUALITY=low, LIGHTS=12      24 frames a second
    1920x1080, QUALITY=high                15 frames a second

  low      Reduced texture sizes, no shadows, no special effects (blood,
           decals, muzzle flashes, shell casings). The fastest.
  medium   Full-size textures and shadows, effects still off.
  high     Full textures, shadows and all the effects.

The processor (Emu68 running the game's 68k code) is the limit more than
the GPU, so smaller screen sizes help less than you might expect.


6. SOUND
--------

The default is the Amiga's own Paula chip, mixed to 8-bit mono at 22 kHz.
It costs little and needs nothing installed. AUDIO=ahi plays through AHI
instead (AHI 6 with a mode set in AHI Prefs), in 16-bit: better
for USB or other sound cards, but it takes more of the processor.

Speech, music and effects all play. There is no reverb or 3D effect
(EAX), as on a PC without it.


7. PLAYING
----------

The controls are Doom 3's own (W A S D to move, the mouse to look and
shoot, Space to jump, C to crouch, F for the flashlight, 1-9 for weapons,
Tab for the PDA); change them in Options > Controls.

  - The console: the key left of 1, below Esc.
  - Saved games and settings: Doom3/save/base/.
  - The game's last output (for problem reports): T:doom3-out.txt, until
    the Amiga is switched off.


8. TROUBLESHOOTING
------------------

Nothing happens when I double-click the icon
  Look at T:doom3-out.txt (e.g. "Type T:doom3-out.txt" in a Shell). It
  holds the game's messages. Common reasons:
  - "... .library failed to load": a system library is missing, or LIBS:
    is not assigned (Assign LIBS: should list SYS:Libs). Reboot.
  - No game data: the pak00?.pk4 files are not in Doom3/base/.

A requester says Doom 3 needs ogles2.library 1.3 or newer
  An older ogles2.library in LIBS: is found before the one in Doom3/libs/.
  Copy Doom3/libs/ogles2.library to LIBS: (and Doom3/libs/v3dglslc too),
  or install ogles2 1.3.1 from its own release.

The screen stays black or the game stops at once
  The screen mode is missing: add a 32-bit mode of that size in
  Picasso96Mode, or start with W= and H= of a mode you have.

The game is much slower than in section 5
  Check the quality (QUALITY=low) and that nothing else is busy. The
  first time a new effect appears the game may stop for a moment while a
  shader is prepared.

The Amiga freezes
  Please report it, with T:doom3-out.txt if you can still read it, what
  you were doing, and your settings.


9. KNOWN LIMITATIONS
--------------------

  - Single player only: there is no networking (multiplayer).
  - The expansion "Resurrection of Evil" (d3xp) is not supported.
  - Lights limited by LIGHTS can pop in and out as you move.
  - Levels take a minute or two to load.
  - Changing the quality in the game's menu takes effect only at the next
    start, and QUALITY is applied at every start.
  - A timedemo with sound off (SOUND=0) crashes; run timedemos with sound.


10. WHAT IS IN THE DRAWER
-------------------------

  Doom3              Starts the game (the icon); runs Doom3.script
  Doom3.script       The settings: screen, quality, sound; then the game
  dhewm3             The game itself
  low.cfg, medium.cfg, high.cfg
                     The three quality settings
  libs/              ogles2.library 1.3 and its shader compiler v3dglslc
  shaders/           The game's shaders, compiled ahead of time
  base/              Doom 3's data goes here (pak000.pk4 - pak008.pk4)
  demo/              Or the free demo's data (demo00.pk4)
  save/              Made at the first start: settings and saved games
  licences/          The licences of the parts
  ReadMe             This text


